diff --git a/docs/source/whats_new.rst b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
index 84278fd204..99e672bc14 100644
--- a/docs/source/whats_new.rst
+++ b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ Version 1.8.0 (2026-10-06)
 Enhancements
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.PerezBlanco2026`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Wang2026` and :class:`moabb.datasets.Han2026` read from NEMAR: PerezBlanco2026 and Wang2026 take the subject's original files from the published deposits ``nm000304`` and ``nm000335`` (``nemar_seed_cache``; Wang2026 declares the deposit's ``sub-<id>`` subject labels), and Han2026 reads NEMAR's raw import of OpenNeuro ds007327 (``on007327``) before OpenNeuro. The private deposits of Brodu2012 (``nm000366``), Lenaig2026 (``nm000333``), MartinezPeon2025 (``nm000332``), MIBMPI2024 (``nm000331``) and MIND2026 (``nm000337``) get their ``nemar_id`` once published (:gh:`1318` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
+- :class:`moabb.datasets.Tavakolan2017`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Liu2025`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Zhou2020` and :class:`moabb.datasets.Wu2020` take the extracted per-subject tree from the NEMAR store (``fill_tree_from_store``) before downloading the per-subject ZIP, so a subject already mirrored in a deposit loads with no upstream request (:gh:`1313` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Add ``n_jobs_data`` to all evaluations (default ``1``, unchanged behavior): it is forwarded as ``n_jobs`` to :meth:`~moabb.paradigms.base.BaseParadigm.get_data`, so subjects are loaded in parallel. :meth:`moabb.datasets.base.BaseDataset.get_data` already supported ``n_jobs`` but evaluations never passed it, so loading was always sequential; this matters when reads are latency-bound, e.g. raw EDF files on a network filesystem (:gh:`1250` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Install a ``moabb`` console script (``[project.scripts] moabb = "moabb.run:main"``), so benchmarks run with ``moabb --pipelines=./pipelines/ --evaluations WithinSession`` instead of ``python -m moabb.run ...``; the command-line logic of :mod:`moabb.run` moved into a reusable ``main(argv=None)`` (:gh:`175` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Test MOABB on free-threaded CPython 3.14 (``3.14t``) with an allowed-to-fail CI job that also checks importing MOABB keeps the GIL disabled, and require ``h5py>=3.16.0`` on Python 3.14+, the first h5py release with free-threaded (``cp314t``) wheels (:gh:`829` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
